\n\n$$\na+b+c=-4+(-9)+20=7.\n$$"] [17592186259626 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix form of $T$ gives us the following information:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}}_{A}\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u}+\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{7\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-4)}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}}_{u} & =\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot (\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}-\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}}_{b}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-7+(-1)+3=-5.\n$$"] [17592186259627 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 